      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T20:09:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It isn\u0027t obvious to me how that would take away functionality?  I think the API choices here are going to generate a lot of confusion, so it would be good to articulate why we cannot go with the more obvious:\n\n1 - expose a LogEntry of type CPER\n2 - use DiagnosticData type of CPER/Section on the above LogEntry\n3 - provide access to the raw log via AdditionalDataUri or DiagnosticData",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a304a0eb959c8f071596d2ff550accd5691d4e72",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1de1506b_1d3da317",
        "filename": "designs/cper-event-logs.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T20:17:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existing LogService uses AdditionalDataURI for the phosphor-logging JSON.  Using that for CPER instead means you don’t have a way to get that existing JSON. \n\nI’m not following #3 in what you wrote above. If the type is CPER you are required that the DiagnosticData (if small enough) and the AdditionalDataURI provide the raw CPER data. We can’t have DD and ADU deviate by Redfish requirements.",
      "parentUuid": "e2566156_9c974897",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a304a0eb959c8f071596d2ff550accd5691d4e72",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72bfe032_01df3110",
        "filename": "designs/cper-event-logs.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T20:39:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assumed you could have different DiagnosticDataType values for different log entries.  Where my brain went was the existing LogEntries for BMC events would keep OEM for the DiagnosticDataType and point at the phosphor-logging JSON.  No functionality lost.  For these new CPER LogEntries, we would use a DiagnosticDataType of CPER/Section and point at the CPER, not the phosphor-logging JSON.\n\nIf you are saying RF clients need the phosphor-logging JSON for CPER LogEntries, then I understand the problem.  If that is the case...\n\nIt seems like we\u0027ve kind of gotten ourselves stuck - using this line of reasoning will we ever be able to implement a DiagnosticDataType other than OEM in our unified/multi-type EventLog?",
      "parentUuid": "1de1506b_1d3da317",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a304a0eb959c8f071596d2ff550accd5691d4e72",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c301089_f7b7be39",
        "filename": "designs/cper-event-logs.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T21:00:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If you are saying RF clients need the phosphor-logging JSON for CPER LogEntries, then I understand the problem. If that is the case...\n\nCorrect.  Because the CPER is just an \"extension\" to an existing event and existing events can have data that is only available by the AD-URI.\n\n\u003e It seems like we\u0027ve kind of gotten ourselves stuck - using this line of reasoning will we ever be able to implement a DiagnosticDataType other than OEM in our unified/multi-type EventLog?\n\nRight, it is unfortunate that we\u0027re \"stuck\" this way.\n\nThat\u0027s why I\u0027m proposing that we have a odata link of some sort over to the CPER-only event.  This could look exactly like the one in the EventLog except that it is of type CPER{Section} and contains the raw CPER data in the AD-URI.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is in any way worse than the \"separate CPER repository\" proposal so while it is not ideal it doesn\u0027t seem unreasonable (in fact it is strictly better than the separate CPER repository because it has both the phosphor-logging and raw CPER representations avaialable).",
      "parentUuid": "72bfe032_01df3110",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 78
      },
